    "get": [
      {
        "id": "WF-406",
        "title": "SUB-1 — Mirror the spec phase to the tracker via two slots",
        "description": "Umbrella: C021 / WF-405 · Type: feat · Complexity: M · Depends on: — (first in the serialized SUB-1 -> SUB-2 -> SUB-3 chain) · Actor: tracker-bound developer / reviewer reading the tracker\n\nObjective\n\nAt spec the tracker gets exactly one read plus one \"Dev\" backfill update and nothing else — no published spec artifact, and open questions never reach the parent. A team watching the tracker sees the task exist but cannot read its spec or its questions.\n\nDeliver: after spec writes 01_spec.md in a Linear-bound project, the tracker carries the umbrella (created or reused) plus a Spec: sub-issue holding the full spec markdown (labelled, set Done as an artifact), and any open questions have been posted as a parent comment before the interactive questioning — with the existing single update reconciled, not duplicated.\n\nScope\n\nIn:\n- Add interface.md to plugins/wf/skills/spec/ (none today) with a ## Slots section declaring spec.publish (merge policy replace) and spec.questions (replace).\n- Insert <!-- wf:slot spec.publish --> (after 01_spec.md is written) and <!-- wf:slot spec.questions --> (before the interactive question block) markers in spec/SKILL.md, each with a no-op inline default.\n- Contribute the spec.publish + spec.questions fragments in wf-linear (ensure umbrella create/reuse; publish Spec: sub-issue Done; post_comment open questions to the parent), bound only to abstract tracker-contract ops.\n- Reconcile with spec's pre-existing single update (Dev backfill) — write per artifact, never double-publish.\n- Version-bump wf core + wf-linear (both plugin.json + marketplace.json) and the top-level marketplace version.\n\nOut: the plan/tasks slots (SUB-2); the implement slots (SUB-3); wf-ado fragments (SUB-4); the bare-core invariant test (SUB-5). Any tracker-contract extension — the five needed ops already exist; a genuinely missing op must be flagged loudly in the umbrella (WF-405), not added silently.\n\nSuccess criteria (acceptance scenarios)\n\n- Given a Linear-bound project and a task folder, when spec completes, then the tracker shows the umbrella plus a Spec: sub-issue containing the full spec markdown set to Done, and the Dev backfill update still runs exactly once (no duplicate spec write).\n- Given open questions arise during spec, when the phase reaches its interactive question block, then those questions appear as a single parent comment on the umbrella before the user is prompted.\n- Given the same run, when skill-slot-marker-lint.sh and validate-skill-interface (D1–D5) run against spec, then both pass and registry validation passes.\n\nConstraints\n\nCore purity (Article #1) — spec/SKILL.md names zero tracker nouns; all publish behavior lives in the wf-linear fragments behind the no-op defaults. Reuse the C014 slot mechanism exactly (## Slots declaration, <!-- wf:slot … --> markers, resolve_content class: slot under precedence _local/slots/spec.<point>.md > pack contribution > inline default), per capability-registry.ops.md §\"Filled-slot resolution at runtime.\" Every change ships a version bump (§8); slot markers are CI-enforced.\n\nVerification evidence\n\nLive Linear end-to-end run showing umbrella + Spec: sub-issue + questions comment; slot lint + validate-skill-interface + registry validation all green; a single-write check confirming the spec item is written once per artifact.",
        "status": "Backlog",
        "parent": "WF-405",
        "labels": []
      },
      {
        "id": "WF-409",
        "title": "SUB-6 — Compose cleanup articles into the constitution and sweep scratch at finalize",
        "description": "Umbrella: C021 / WF-405 · Type: feat · Complexity: M · Depends on: — (parallel-capable; rebase-then-merge on shared version files) · Actor: any developer / reviewer relying on \"nothing left behind\"\n\nObjective\n\nThe prototype's \"nothing left behind\" promise is unported: the constitution's scratch-placement article states only where scratch lives, with no lifecycle/sweep obligation, and tf leaves scratch residue behind at finalize.\n\nDeliver: the constitution payload's scratch-placement article (core Article #9) is extended with a domain-free lifecycle clause stating both ported tmp-contract obligations explicitly — (a) per-consumer immediate deletion (each scratch file deleted the moment its consumer skill has run, not deferred to a later sweep) and (b) breadcrumb deletion by the run-ending skill — composed verbatim with core provenance; and tf sweeps scratch residue at finalize as the backstop for any residue those two obligations do not already remove, so no _local/scratch (.tmp) residue remains.\n\nScope\n\nIn:\n- Extend core Article #9 in the constitution payload (the C015 mechanism) with a lifecycle clause stating both obligations explicitly (per-consumer immediate deletion + breadcrumb deletion by the run-ending skill), authored as a domain-free core process article, composed verbatim, with the tf finalize sweep named as the backstop, not a substitute for either obligation.\n- Add a scratch sweep to plugins/wf/skills/tf/SKILL.md that removes any residual scratch at finalize (the backstop), obeying the \"never write outside _local/\" rule.\n- Confirm /wf:constitution composes the new clause with core provenance.\n- Version-bump wf core (constitution payload + tf) plus the top-level marketplace version.\n\nOut: the seven bookkeeping slots (SUB-1/2/3); any tracker behavior; capability-authored articles (this clause is core, domain-free).\n\nSuccess criteria (acceptance scenarios)\n\n- Given a task with scratch residue under _local/scratch/, when tf finalizes, then no .tmp scratch residue remains and the sweep writes nothing outside _local/.\n- Given /wf:constitution runs, when the constitution is composed, then the extended Article #9 clause appears verbatim with core provenance and states both obligations — per-consumer immediate deletion and breadcrumb deletion by the run-ending skill — with the tf finalize sweep named only as the backstop (the clause cannot pass while asserting a single vague sweep obligation).\n\nConstraints\n\nCleanup articles are domain-free core process articles composed verbatim (C015 payload mechanism); the tf sweep obeys \"never write outside _local/\" (§6). Every change ships a version bump. Parallel-capable but rebase-then-merge on the shared wf-core version pair + top-level marketplace version.\n\nVerification evidence\n\nPost-run check showing no _local/scratch .tmp residue after tf; composed constitution showing the new clause under core provenance and carrying both obligations verbatim (per-consumer immediate deletion + breadcrumb deletion, tf sweep as backstop).",
        "status": "Backlog",
        "parent": "WF-405",
        "labels": []
      },
      {
        "id": "WF-405",
        "title": "C021 slice — tracker mirror + constitution cleanup",
        "description": "A two-item backlog slice covering two independent, parallel-capable feature enhancements: mirroring one authoring phase to the tracker via declared slots, and composing a cleanup convention into the project's shared constitution payload plus a matching finalize-time sweep.",
